After finally collecting all the source, I want to compile my own
NetHack 3.0i for the Amiga.  A few hours of this has yielded nothing
but frustration.  I will spare the problem descriptions and get to the
point:

I have just today acquired Aztec C 5.0a for the Amiga.  There are a
bunch of hints for Aztec 3.6 in the INSTALL.AMI file, but nothing
about the 5.0a version.

The makefile has allowances for 3.6, but NOTHING for 5.0.  In fact,
the default arguments (CCFLAGS) there are for 3.6, and these are not
compatible with the 5.0 arguments.  What's more, the 5.0 manual does
not describe the old arguments, so I can not figure out what they do.
At best, I can stick a "-3" in the line to force 3.6 style argument
interpretation.

There are LOTS of allowances in the code for 5.0.  These are mostly
things like #ifdef AZTEC_50.  The Mac uses a similar compiler (I
think), but these seemed to be allowances for the Amiga.  This leads
me to believe that someone has actually compiled the thing
successfully.

Can someone experienced with this compile help out?  These sorts of
things would be most helpful:

A step-by-step listing of everything you did to get this to compile
(yeah, right).

What needs to be done for 5.0 as opposed to 3.6 (Is the diskzap still
necessary?  What about variable arguments?  Bitfields?  defined()?
That macro for abbreviating object descriptions?).

Is there a newer version of the installation instructions?  The ones I
have date to patch level 7, but the code is level 9.  What about a
newer makefile?

Any other helpful tips....

Please E-mail.  I will summarize.  If there are any requests, I will post.

